   "final_rule_text": "Each model must undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C using a regulator-approved protocol and a statistically representative sample. The maximum failure rate is 5%. A model exceeding 5% may be sold only under regulator-approved corrective action and safeguards, with retesting on a regulator-set schedule; regulators may require immediate measures or prohibit sales at any rate where evidence indicates a serious safety risk. Manufacturers shall submit complete per-model results, including exact failure rates, to the regulator. Customers who buy or own the model must receive its pass/fail status, exact per-model failure rate, and material safety information. Results need not be published to the general public."
