   "comparison": "all parameters acceptable or better",
   "final_rule_text": "Before purchase and throughout ownership, customers must receive accessible safety notices covering safe installation and use, known material risks, incident trends, the model’s 55 °C thermal-test status, its exact per-model failure rate, and required precautions. Regulators shall receive complete per-model thermal-test results, including exact failure rates. Results need not be published to the general public. Manufacturers must promptly notify affected customers and regulators of a material safety defect and provide clear mitigation instructions. A mandatory recall is triggered when any model exceeds 8 thermal incidents per 100,000 installed units in a year. The manufacturer must promptly stop sales, notify affected customers and regulators, and offer an effective remedy, which may include repair or replacement. Following corrective action, sales may resume when the regulator determines the safety issue has been adequately addressed. Regulators may require a recall at a lower rate where evidence indicates an imminent or serious risk."
